            <persName type="full">W[illiam] L[eonard] Courtney</persName>
            <date type="birth" when="1850-01-05"/>
            <date type="death" when="1928-11-01"/>
            <note type="gender">M</note>
         </ab>
         <div type="bio">
            <p>English editor and journalist. Courtney attended Oxford and was elected to a fellowship there. Beginning in the 1880s, he began writing for the British press, and in 1890 left Oxford to become chief dramatic and literary editor for the <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Daily Telegraph</name>, where he stayed until 1925. He was also editor of the <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Fortnightly Review</name> from 1894 to 1928. While in that capacity, he accepted JJ’s first publication, “Ibsen’s New Drama” (67, no. 400  [1 April 1900]: 575-90). JJ visited Courtney in London the following month. <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
